I know a thing or two about software licenses, and I detest the kind
of misinformation that seems to surround them so often.   I don't
understand where the notion comes into play that one can be granted a
right to distribute a piece of work, while somehow not reserving the
right to do so for consideration.  Such a provision would require a
contract, not merely a license, because it seeks to take a right away
from another party.  A license can only grant rights that would
otherwise be reserved to the granting party, it cannot abridge any
rights of any other party.



